NanoDPU RPMB factory environment
==============================

The AN7583 kernel includes a read-only eMMC RPMB NVMEM provider. It is
enabled only for MMC cards with an "rpmb" child whose compatible is
"mmc-rpmb-nvmem". Other cards are unaffected.

The provider exposes the RPMB data capacity as bytes, excluding protocol
headers. It reads one 256-byte data block per transaction, supports
unaligned reads spanning blocks, and checks transport errors, response
type, result, address and nonce. It does not verify response MACs and
must not be used as an authenticated or confidential storage interface.
It exposes no data-write or key-programming operation.

NanoDPU uses the existing u-boot,env NVMEM layout with env-size = <256>.
The environment starts at RPMB data block zero. Its four-byte little-endian
CRC32 covers the remaining 252 bytes, including padding. Generate it with:

  mkenvimage -s 0x100 -o factory-env.bin factory-env.txt

Example text input:

  ethaddr=8A:43:A7:2B:3B:BE
  serial#=7
  model=NanoDPU

Provision the environment separately using your existing RPMB tooling.
The kernel does not provision it or modify any RPMB contents. Reserve this
block for factory data; it must not overlap storage owned by a TEE.

The layout validates the CRC and creates a cell for each variable. The
ethaddr cell converts the ASCII MAC to six bytes and supplies GDM2/eth0.
GDM3/eth1 uses the base MAC plus one. Serial and model are
exported as strings; this does not replace the device-tree model or
automatically populate the system serial-number property.

Read-only checks after boot:

  dmesg | grep -Ei 'rpmb|nvmem|CRC|eth0'
  ls /sys/bus/nvmem/devices/
  cat /sys/class/net/eth0/address
  ls /sys/bus/nvmem/devices/rpmb*-nvmem/cells/
  cat /sys/bus/nvmem/devices/rpmb*-nvmem/cells/serial\#@*
  cat /sys/bus/nvmem/devices/rpmb*-nvmem/cells/model@*
  dd if=/sys/bus/nvmem/devices/rpmb0-nvmem/nvmem bs=256 count=1 | hexdump -C

The expected eth0 address for the example is 8a:43:a7:2b:3b:be. The serial
and model cells contain 7 and NanoDPU, without terminating newlines.
The RPMB device number may differ if multiple devices are present.

If the RPMB key is not provisioned, or a transaction fails, reads return
an error. A bad environment CRC prevents creation of the layout cells.
The CRC detects corruption but does not authenticate the environment.
